#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:3
msgid "Convention for implementing entrypoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:5
msgid ""
"The implementations of LLVM-libc entrypoints live in the `src/` directory, "
"organized by the public header they belong to. Some entrypoints are "
"platform- specific, and so their implementations are in a subdirectory with "
"the name of the platform (e.g., `stdio/linux/remove.cpp`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:10
msgid ""
"For a complete overview of what an entrypoint is and how it is managed in "
"the build system, see the {ref}`entrypoints` documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:13
msgid ""
"Implementation of entrypoints can span multiple `.cpp` and `.h` files, but "
"there will be at least one header file with name of the form `<entrypoint "
"name>.h` for every entrypoint. This header file is called the implementation "
"header file. For the `isalpha` function, the path to the implementation "
"header file is `src/ctype/isalpha.h`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:19
msgid "Implementation Header File Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:21
msgid ""
"We will use the `isalpha` function from the public `ctype.h` header file as "
"an example. The `isalpha` function will be declared in an internal header "
"file `src/ctype/isalpha.h` as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:39
msgid ""
"All LLVM-libc implementation constructs must be enclosed in the "
"`LIBC_NAMESPACE_DECL` namespace. See {ref}`code_style` for the full "
"technical rationale and macro definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:43
msgid "`.cpp` File Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:45
msgid ""
"The main `.cpp` file is named `<entrypoint name>.cpp` and is usually in the "
"same folder as the header. It contains the signature of the entrypoint "
"function, which must be defined with the `LLVM_LIBC_FUNCTION` macro. For "
"example, the `isalpha` function from `ctype.h` is defined as follows, in the "
"file `src/ctype/isalpha.cpp`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:63
msgid ""
"Notice the use of the macro `LLVM_LIBC_FUNCTION`. This macro helps us define "
"a C alias symbol for the C++ implementation. For example, for a library "
"build, the macro is defined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:77
msgid ""
"The LLVM_LIBC_FUNCTION_ATTR macro is normally defined to nothing, but can be "
"defined by vendors who want to set their own attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/implementation_standard.md:80
msgid "When defining a variable, use the `LLVM_LIBC_VARIABLE` macro:"
msgstr ""
